ng at the correction, make your own attempt using the exact question provided. Compare your working with the feedback: did you use the same skill and show your reasoning? If a digit or place is uncertain, identify what would have to be regrouped or counted again. One deliberate, justified revision is more useful than writing a longer answer.","icon":"📖","notice":"Repeating the worked example cannot show transfer to new numbers. Correct the value or method, not just the appearance of the digits.","title":"Transfer to a new problem"}],"title":"Year 4, Week 36, Lesson 1: Grid references and maps","unit_number":9,"unit_title":"Angles, shapes and transformations","week":36,"week_in_unit":4,"word_challenges":null,"worked_example":"WORK THROUGH THIS\nCell B3 means column B, row 3 (confirm the key). Moving right increases the letter/column; moving up increases the row number on many maps.\n\nWrite what makes this example accurate, naming the places, values or distances used.","worked_visuals":[{"alt":"Grid references on maps.","caption":"Do not swap order.","svg":"<svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" viewBox=\"0 0 660 150\"><rect x=\"10\" y=\"12\" width=\"310\" height=\"126\" rx=\"14\" fill=\"#fff4ea\" stroke=\"#b87445\"/><rect x=\"340\" y=\"12\" width=\"310\" height=\"126\" rx=\"14\" fill=\"#e8f5ed\" stroke=\"#297a61\"/><g font-size=\"16\" fill=\"#263948\"><text x=\"28\" y=\"42\">Grid ref</text><text x=\"28\" y=\"78\">letter + number</text><text x=\"358\" y=\"42\">Order</text><text x=\"358\" y=\"78\">agreed key</text></g></svg>"},{"alt":"Correct cell vs swapped ref.","caption":"Twenty locates.","svg":"<svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" viewBox=\"0 0 660 150\"><rect x=\"10\" y=\"12\" width=\"310\" height=\"126\" rx=\"14\" fill=\"#fff4ea\" stroke=\"#b87445\"/><rect x=\"340\" y=\"12\" width=\"310\" height=\"126\" rx=\"14\" fill=\"#e8f5ed\" stroke=\"#297a61\"/><g font-size=\"16\" fill=\"#263948\"><text x=\"28\" y=\"42\">C2 → D2</text><text x=\"28\" y=\"78\">one rig